\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Architectural comparison across four query-time table--text reasoning paradigms. This comparison strictly evaluates query-time evidence construction and inference over ad-hoc inputs, excluding offline corpus-wide pre-indexing (e.g., GraphRAG, HippoRAG\nobreakspace  {}2) and parametric model training or fine-tuning (e.g., HYBRIDER, MuGER²). In contrast to unguided linear prompt concatenation\nobreakspace  {}(a), destructive question-driven graph pruning in online KGs like ODYSSEY\nobreakspace  {}(b), and expensive multi-turn agentic exploration over online KGs in systems like HydraRAG and ToG-3\nobreakspace  {}(c), the proposed QEG-RAG framework\nobreakspace  {}(d) dynamically instantiates a schema-preserving online multigraph on-the-fly, retains complete evidence context, guides attention via deterministic multi-factor scored paths, and resolves bottlenecks via a bounded two-tier diagnostic-driven execution protocol.}}{4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:paradigms}{{1}{4}}
