\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Two-tier controlled reasoning engine (Stage\nobreakspace  {}3) structured as two parallel algorithmic blocks with deterministic graph compression, illustrated via the running AFL example. (Left) Tier\nobreakspace  {}1 evaluates the unpruned evidence graph under guided path scaffolding. When candidate evidence is unambiguous, execution terminates via Fast Exit in a single LLM call ($\approx 80\%$ of queries). When candidate collision occurs (e.g., both Toronto Eagles and Toronto Blues formed in 1989), the LLM emits a structured diagnostic packet. (Center to Right) An automated zero-LLM search fetches targeted bridge passages and executes algorithmic graph compression ($\approx 85\%$ size reduction), discarding non-competing candidates to construct the minimal state capsule. In Tier\nobreakspace  {}2, the LLM resolves the ambiguity deterministically by factual evidence in a targeted second call (at most 2 calls total), producing the verified answer with full provenance.}}{9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:two-tier}{{3}{9}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{Diagnostic Handoff and Targeted Bridge Augmentation.}{9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{eq:targeted-retrieval}{{5}{9}}
